  "description": "KOSTAL Smart Energy Meter (KSEM) as Modbus RTU slave (RS485 A/B) or Modbus TCP slave (port 502): internal OBIS power and energy registers",
  "revision": 2,
  "revised": "2026-10-17",
  "source": "KOSTAL Solar Electric, \"KOSTAL Smart Energy Meter - Modbus interface description\" (BA KOSTAL Interface KSEM EN)",
  "sources": [{"title": "KOSTAL Smart Energy Meter Interface description", "url": "https://www.kostal-solar-electric.com/fileadmin/downloadcenter/kse/BA_KOSTAL_Interface_KSEM_EN.pdf", "note": "Sections 3.2 and 3.3: internal instantaneous and energy registers"}],
  "notes": [
    "Registers are read with FC03. Multi-register values are big-endian, high word first; request all registers of a value in one read.",
    "Modbus TCP slave listens on port 502 (802 with TLS). The RS-485 ports are configured in the web interface; the document gives no serial defaults.",
    "Power values are split into + (import) and - (export) registers, each unsigned.",
    "Unlisted registers return exception 0x02. Not in this map: the KSEM/RM PnP block (8192 onwards), the SunSpec block (40000-40177), and the energy flow, wallbox, group and sensor blocks."
  ],
